response.text:
The issue was that `parseRange` did not handle cases where only a single number was provided. When `text.split("-")` is called on a string without a hyphen, it returns an array with one element, leaving the `to` variable as `undefined`. Calling `Number(undefined)` results in `NaN`.

I updated `parse-range.mjs` to check if `to` is `undefined` and, if so, set it to the value of `from`.

```javascript
export function parseRange(text) {
  const [from, to] = text.split("-");
  return { from: Number(from), to: to === undefined ? Number(from) : Number(to) };
}
```
